Orders text that mixes HarfBuzz-shaped sections with glyph PBF sections, and
shapes each script of a right-to-left run on its own. A label whose font-faces
cover some of its characters lays out in sections, and shaping ran bidi on each
glyph PBF section alone, then joined the sections in logical order. A label
such as "هەولێر Erbil" or "شارع 12" put its Latin word or digits on the wrong
side. Now the lines are split in logical order and the whole text is reordered
at once, with each shaped section seen as characters of its direction and moved
as a block. A right-to-left run that holds two scripts, such as Hebrew and
Arabic under one font face, was shaped as the first script, which left the
Arabic letters unjoined. Now each script is shaped on its own, and the parts are
laid out right to left. The bidi tests now build: their CMake condition read
the string "MBGL_WITH_QT" instead of the MLN_WITH_QT option, which left them out
of every build.
Issue: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/issues/4513
Upstream: not proposed

